erve howfar-7is from 0 and how far+7 is from O using thenumber line.", "conf": 0.853, "box": [[123, 1363], [1394, 1379], [1393, 1418], [122, 1401]]}, {"text": "Look at the numberlinebelow.", "conf": 0.872, "box": [[125, 1419], [593, 1426], [593, 1459], [124, 1452]]}, {"text": "-10-9 -8  -6 -5 -4 -3 -2 -1 0", "conf": 0.764, "box": [[212, 1546], [832, 1556], [831, 1599], [211, 1589]]}, {"text": "10", "conf": 0.579, "box": [[1363, 1573], [1414, 1573], [1414, 1609], [1363, 1609]]}, {"text": "Here, -7 is 7 steps away from 0 to its left. +7 is also 7 steps away from 0 but to its right. So", "conf": 0.938, "box": [[123, 1617], [1533, 1649], [1532, 1698], [122, 1666]]}, {"text": "the distance of -7 and +7 from zero is the same but in the opposite directions.", "conf": 0.926, "box": [[122, 1667], [1340, 1695], [1339, 1744], [121, 1716]]}, {"text": "In Mathematics, this distance of -7 and +7 from 0 on the number line is known as its", "conf": 0.927, "box": [[123, 1719], [1447, 1752], [1446, 1800], [122, 1767]]}, {"text": "absolute value.Absolute value of an integer is always positive.", "conf": 0.888, "box": [[125, 1774], [1088, 1796], [1087, 1839], [124, 1817]]}, {"text": "There are two features of integers.", "conf": 0.854, "box": [[127, 1829], [642, 1840], [642, 1876], [126, 1865]]}, {"text": "32", "conf": 0.561, "box": [[772, 1947], [823, 1947], [823, 1987], [772, 1987]]}, {"text": "NOTFORSALE", "conf": 0.777, "box": [[1128, 1965], [1416, 1975], [1415, 2005], [1127, 1995]]}]}